RobWork/doc/sphinx\manual\inverse_kinematics.rst:32:This robot has 6 degrees of freedom, and the solver will provide up to 8 solutions.
RobWork/doc/sphinx\manual\inverse_kinematics.rst:33:Notice that for every joint there is a solution where the joint is rotated 360 degrees.
RobWork/doc/sphinx\manual\inverse_kinematics.rst:34:Than means that each of the 8 solutions can typically be achieved in 64 different ways. It is up to the user to add or subtract 360 degrees such that it suits the application best.
RobWork/doc/sphinx\manual\inverse_kinematics.rst:40:This robot has 7 degrees of freedom. It can have an infinite number of solutions, as the middle joint can be placed anywhere on a circle.
RobWork/doc/sphinx\manual\inverse_kinematics.rst:48:The rw::invkin::PieperSolver is a closed form solver that works for serial devices with 6 degrees of freedom revolute joints. It requires that the last three axes intersect.
